  partName: Engine Block
  description: The Engine Block is a large, complex component made of Frame material,
    located at the middle-center-center of the engine, serving as the main structural
    and functional element of the engine. Its size and shape provide a foundation
    for the engine's cylinders, pistons, and crankshaft, while its material offers
    strength and durability. Notably, the Engine Block is designed with a series
    of passageways and chambers to facilitate coolant and oil circulation.
